From: SoundTap contributors <soundtap@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wlconf: return 0 from write_file on success

write_file returned an uninitialised ret after a successful write, so
wlconf -C exited non-zero (255 on arm64) although the output was written.

Upstream: not sent, 18xx-ti-utils is no longer developed
Signed-off-by: Stein Milder <info@steinmilder.nl>
---
--- a/wlconf/main.c
+++ b/wlconf/main.c
@@ -575,6 +575,7 @@
 	}
 
 	fclose(file);
+	ret = 0;
 out:
 	return ret;
 }
